That's cool.

Pure anecdote: I'm not one of the top 5-10 players in the world, but I
have ascended a 6-in-a-row streak in a tournament at one point (and by
Z-score I'm ranked #18 on NAO, for what little that deeply flawed
metric matters) and I've talked to several players who are far better
than me.  Based on those conversations, I think leaving Magicbane at
+2 is a stupid rookie mistake.  But I could easily be wrong, and you
should certainly look for more compelling statistical arguments (my
personal experience is certainly based on a statistically
insignificant sample size).  All I can do is relate what I've found to
work well for me.

I do think that the +2 recommendation is based on a fairly silly
analysis that made it into a spoiler at one point.  But I certainly
don't have anything approaching rock-solid evidence supporting that
belief.

Certainly if you hang out with the players who are a lot better than
me, though, you'll hear that they like enchanting it as much as
possible.  Good enough for me, given that it coincides with my
experience.  I've never heard any of the elite players advocate
leaving it at +2, and I have spent a fair bit of time hanging out in
IRC chat rooms with them.


